  Double damage with the spell of magic missile.  The damage 
magic missile does per hit depends on [(XL/2) +1].  You're
current XP level is 14.  That gives a factor of 8.  

  So right now your base damage per hit with magic missile is
8 d6.  That's shorthand for eight six-sided dice rolled.
The average result of a six-sided die roll is 3.5.

  So your base magic missile damage should average 28 points per
hit.  You get a bonus of 1 for having Int of 18, average/hit = 29.

  That's not bad.  If you keep increasing your level you can
keep increasing the damage done by magic missile.  Bump your Int
as well.

  You'd max out at (16 d6 ) +2.  That averages out to (16 * 3.5) +2
which gives 58 points of damage per hit.  (Yes, you'll face slightly
tougher monsters at XL 30.)

  Oh, yeah, did I mention that the Magic Mirror of Merlin doubles
that damage for knights?  So *right now* magic missile will do 58
points of damage per hit for you.


  And you can use magic missile:
    - to hit monsters at range (before they can hit you back).
    - to reflect and hit monsters around corners.
    - to hit multiple monsters per cast.
    - to reflect and hit the same monster several times.
    - to kill monsters without damaging their inventory/death-drops.


